<title>USA: KOCH cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>KOCH cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.50 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $20.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana Sweet crude is now $22.50 a barrel, and Oklahoma Sweet is $22.50.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
